  "body": "Background batch gate on main at d612583 (after PR #138, #106 footprint rings) is red: 960 passed, 7 failed, all lathe.\n\n- lathe_post::facing_posts_to_the_lathe_golden: the warnings in facing.nc differ (the inward rapids 1/5/9/13/17 versus the golden)\n- turning_bore::a_bored_op_runs_clean_in_the_document, ::the_bore_seed_stands, ::a_regrind_of_the_nose_convicts_through_the_digest: RapidInStock { at: 18 }\n- turning_contour::a_chamfered_face_rides_clean_in_the_document, ::the_seeds_of_the_contour_kinds_stand: RapidInStock { at: 55 }; ::a_nose_regrind_marks_the_rides_stale_both_ways\n\nCause (inferred from the merge list, not bisected): #106's milling footprint (8 rings, tip lift) now judges a turning op's radial rapids in the lathe frame. The turning ops' rapids are not milling-tool rapids. PR #138's gate ran the verify-calling app suites but not the turning suites, so it missed this.\n\nNot a gouge: these are false refusals (or golden drift) of lathe programs, so P1. The fix rides PR #135 (#103), whose meridian law is meant to own turning rapids. The column/footprint law should not judge a turning op's rapids at all, and #135's merge of main already reproduces the facing case.\n\nLogs: gate-logs/batch-20261107-225237 in the main checkout.",
